---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const nav = `<strong>Start</strong><a href="/docs">Overview</a><a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a><strong>Build</strong><a href="/docs/api">API reference</a><a href="/docs/integrations" class="active">SDK &amp; frameworks</a><a href="/docs/multilingual">Multilingual</a><strong>Run</strong><a href="/docs/hosting">Hosting</a><a href="/docs/security">Security</a>`;
---
<Base title="Memflex integrations — SDK, LangGraph, voice, tools, guardrails" desc="Five patterns covering nearly every agent, including LiveKit voice agents." path="/docs/integrations">
<div class="wrap" style="padding:64px 24px">
  <span class="eyebrow">Docs · Integrations</span>
  <h1>Five patterns, every agent.</h1>
  <div class="docs-grid" style="margin-top:30px">
    <nav class="docs-nav" set:html={nav}></nav>
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>1 · One-liner SDK</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>from reflex.plug import openai_client  # or anthropic_client
chat = openai_client()  # REFLEX_URL env → your server
r = chat.chat.completions.create(model="mock/mock-echo",
    messages=[&#123;"role": "user", "content": "Hi"&#125;], user="u1")</pre></div>
      <p>Raw client: <code>from reflex import Client; Client("http://localhost:8000").ask(...)</code></p>
      <h2>2 · LangGraph node</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>from reflex.contrib.langgraph import MemflexNode  # (ReflexNode alias kept)
graph.add_node("respond", MemflexNode(llm="mock/mock-echo"))</pre></div>
      <h2>3 · Tool-agents (plan once, serve forever)</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>res = rx.ask(user_id=u, message=q, llm=llm)
if res.source.startswith("reflex"):
    return res.answer                 # zero tools, zero LLM
facts = run_tools(plan(llm, q))       # System 2, miss only
composed = " | ".join(facts)
rx.save_reflex(user_id=u, message=q, answer=composed)  # upsert, no dupes</pre></div>
      <h2>4 · Guardrail gate (typed + confident only)</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>res = rx.ask(..., extract_structured=True,
             output_schema=&#123;"refund_status": "str"&#125;)
if res.source.startswith("reflex") and res.confidence &gt;= 0.9:
    auto_approve(res)   # calibrated safe band
else:
    escalate_to_human(res)</pre></div>
      <h2>5 · Voice agents (LiveKit)</h2>
      <p>Memflex speaks OpenAI-protocol SSE, so LiveKit's OpenAI plugin connects with a <code>base_url</code> — no custom integration. Repeats stream from memory in milliseconds (ideal for turn-taking); novel turns fall through to your upstream model. Pass the caller identity as <code>user</code> for per-caller memory isolation.</p>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>from livekit.plugins import openai
session = AgentSession(
    llm=openai.LLM(
        model="openai/gpt-4o-mini",  # upstream, used only on misses
        base_url="http://localhost:8000/v1",
        api_key="not-needed",  # or MEMFLEX_API_KEY
        user="caller-123",  # per-caller memory isolation
    ),
    # ... tts, stt, vad, turn_detection, etc.
)</pre></div>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>import * as openai from '@livekit/agents-plugin-openai';
const session = new voice.AgentSession(&#123;
  llm: new openai.LLM(&#123;
    model: 'openai/gpt-4o-mini',
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8000/v1',
    apiKey: 'not-needed',
    user: 'caller-123',
  &#125;),
&#125;);</pre></div>
      <p>Limits, stated plainly: Chat Completions path only (no Realtime/Responses API yet); function tools forward on OpenAI-compatible models, other backends answer explicit 400; keep answers short for voice — the default system prompt already asks for concision.</p>
      <h2>Migrating from Mem0?</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>from reflex.compat import mem0  # basic add/search drop-in
db = mem0.MemoryClient(base_url="http://localhost:8000")</pre></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</Base>
